WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.380
Hi, this is Fernando.

2
00:00:01.380 --> 00:00:04.570
If you have never used AWS, this video is for you.

3
00:00:04.780 --> 00:00:06.070
The idea is simple.

4
00:00:06.280 --> 00:00:09.890
You learn by testing, not by memorizing service names.

5
00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:12.380
AI sits next to you, as a tutor.

6
00:00:12.380 --> 00:00:14.450
But you are the one who writes and decides.

7
00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:16.180
Here's how it works.

8
00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:18.560
First, a real question, in your own words.

9
00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:20.320
Then, a small test.

10
00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:22.080
Next, you keep the evidence:

11
00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:24.000
what you expected and what happened.

12
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:26.100
Finally, you write an article about it.

13
00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:28.110
Each mission takes about one hour.

14
00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:30.240
There are three missions.

15
00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:31.960
In the first, the question is:

16
00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:34.140
will I spend money by accident?

17
00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:37.060
In the second: how do I put a site online safely?

18
00:00:37.060 --> 00:00:39.540
In the third: what does this error mean?

19
00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:42.430
Start with the one that answers your question today.

20
00:00:42.820 --> 00:00:46.170
And you don't need an AWS account to start.

21
00:00:46.360 --> 00:00:49.090
The first steps of every mission run without one.

22
00:00:49.460 --> 00:00:52.100
With one command, you can already check a sample cost

23
00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:54.250
report, with fictional data.

24
00:00:54.560 --> 00:00:58.060
If you move to AWS later, every mission shows you how to

25
00:00:58.060 --> 00:00:59.470
clean up what you created.

26
00:00:59.853 --> 00:01:01.253
There's just one rule.

27
00:01:01.253 --> 00:01:03.973
AI is the tutor. It asks questions,

28
00:01:03.973 --> 00:01:05.513
reviews and explains.

29
00:01:05.513 --> 00:01:08.533
But it makes mistakes, and catching them is part of the

30
00:01:08.533 --> 00:01:10.633
exercise. So check the numbers,

31
00:01:10.633 --> 00:01:13.163
open the links and write in your own words.

32
00:01:13.333 --> 00:01:14.143
Shall we start?

33
00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:16.500
One note before we finish.

34
00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:19.100
The voice you just heard was generated from my cloned

35
00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:21.140
voice, with my authorization.

36
00:01:21.140 --> 00:01:23.120
And this is an independent project.

37
00:01:23.120 --> 00:01:25.990
It is not official AWS material.
